  "updated": "2026-11-17",
  "intro": "Goodbudget, Quicken Simplifi, PocketGuard, Tiller, Monarch Money, and Copilot Money are six YNAB alternatives, with published prices ranging from a $0 free tier on Goodbudget to $199.99 per year on Monarch Money Plus. At The Modern Wallet, we lay out the arithmetic behind subscription costs and feature tiers so people can compare yearly software expenses accurately.\n\n[YNAB](https://www.ynab.com/pricing) charges $109 United States Dollars (USD) per year when paid annually, which equals $9.08 per month, or $14.99 per month on its monthly plan, plus sales tax where applicable. YNAB pairs account connections with an envelope-style budgeting method where users assign every dollar a job. A single YNAB subscription can be shared with up to six people across partners, families, and close-knit groups, and new signups start with a 34-day free trial that requires no credit card.\n\nFor readers exploring broader tools, our [best budgeting apps roundup](/roundup/best-budgeting-apps/) covers general category options, and our [best budgeting apps for couples roundup](/roundup/best-budgeting-apps-for-couples/) compares account-sharing setups. If you want to calculate categories before selecting software, see our [zero-based budget calculator](/budget/zero-based-budget-calculator/) and our guide on [how to make a budget](/guides/how-to-make-a-budget/).",
